<urn:atm:triage:finding/FNX-025>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "FNX-025" ;
  triage:title "No operator control over the nudge-path state machines -- needs one durable task-queue-nudge automation control under the two-machine design" ;
  triage:description "Originates from Rand directly (relayed by fenix, not from her review): \"I want several simple state machines. and I need to be able to stop the additional interconnected state machines that are getting executed.\" fenix verified the basis independently before filing: grepped the workspace for any disable/enable/pause/quiet-hours config, env var, or flag reaching herdr_queue_wake, herdr_escalation, or the attention store -- there is none. tick_once (herdr_queue_wake.rs:246) runs the whole chain unconditionally every tick. The only granularity an operator has today is stopping the daemon entirely. Required outcome: durable, observable, restart-stable operator controls -- atm doctor should print which control(s) are live -- where OFF/Disabled means the affected work is never materialized (not materialized-then-discarded). CURRENT SHAPE (v2, superseded from the original seven-to-four proposal by solar's re-ruling against Rand's actual two-machine specification): the task-queue nudge path has exactly two domain machines -- roster ephemeral member state (presence) and task lifecycle (Assigned/Active) -- and a nudge is a derived, durably queued action, not a third domain state machine. The entire shared attention scheduler (AttentionLane, attention_lane_cursors, multi-lane fairness, reservation status/retry/lease/fence/finalize/tombstone machinery, release_streaks, attention-owned escalation) is being deleted and replaced, not consolidated, so the original attention-global/lane/escalation control proposal is withdrawn along with the machines it would have controlled. What replaces it: ONE durable task-queue-nudge automation control, preferably gating the Idle and Close triggers independently if Rand needs selective stopping, default enabled. Disabled means no new derived nudge work is materialized. Existing already-queued work's disposition on disable (pause-and-resume vs cancel) must be stated explicitly in the design, not left implicit. If ephemeral unread-message nudges remain as an independent path (open question for Rand, per solar), they stay on the existing pending-message delivery path and do not need shared-scheduler machinery preserved just for coexistence. Routing is to solar for the replacement design (an ADR record citing Rand's original direct message/issue, not fenix's relay, per solar's classification), not arch-ctm or cipher, and this finding must not be dispatched to any dev agent until that design is published. CDR-009 is explicitly unaffected by (i.e., orthogonal to, not gated by) this finding; conversely this finding does not gate on CDR-009 either since that whole model is being replaced." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-az" ;
  triage:triageMode "followup_pass" ;
  triage:category "operability" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "crates/atm-http-runtime/src/herdr_queue_wake.rs, crates/atm-http-runtime/src/herdr_queue_wake_escalation.rs, crates/atm-core/src/commands/doctor (or equivalent atm doctor surface), plus whatever new durable nudge/outbox module solar's replacement design introduces" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-10T22:25:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AZ.4 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-10T22:23:29Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/FNX-025/AZ4-001> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "2" .

